{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3180","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3180","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3180\",\"parent_revision\":\"43134b8c5298aef05d3a2024dc934d6c3ba636c8\",\"root_revision\":\"029719a240882c8a58f372316f74ac468341ccffac3729cf2745ffa8908ffe26\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-23\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/unit/progressive_markdown/test_indexer_decomposition.py::TestPLRLintGate::test_indexer_build_passes_plr_complexity_gates` invokes `ruff` as a bare executable rather than through `uv run ruff`. In an environment where ruff is only available via uv (no ruff on PATH), the test fails with `FileNotFoundError: 'ruff'`.\\n\\nReproduced 2026-08-23 by a subagent, which then applied reproduction-integrity discipline: it stashed all its changes and re-ran the same test on unmodified `d402117bf`, getting the identical `FileNotFoundError`. So the cause is environmental and pre-existing, not related to any branch change.\\n\\nWorth noting the observation is not stable across runs \u2014 a separate full-suite run of the same tree on the same machine did not surface this failure and instead surfaced the two order-dependent `test_network_guard` tests tracked in #3179. Both runs totalled 3467 tests. That suggests the visible failure set varies with `pytest-xdist` worker assignment (`-n auto --dist loadgroup`), which may mean this test's environment sensitivity interacts with worker startup, or simply that different workers inherit different PATHs.\\n\\nWhy this matters rather than being ignorable: `.claude/rules/astral-tool-overrides.md` states that tools must be invoked as `uv run <tool>` and never as a bare binary, because a bare invocation resolves a different version than the one CI gates against. A test that shells out to bare `ruff` violates that rule and, when it does find a binary, may be asserting against a different ruff version than the project pins.\\n\\nImpact if left: a failure that appears and disappears between runs trains readers to dismiss failures on sight. During this session that dismissal habit was demonstrated repeatedly, and a genuine regression appearing alongside a known-noisy failure could be waved through the same way.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the obvious direction is to invoke ruff through `uv run` inside the test, matching the repo-wide rule \u2014 but whether the test should shell out at all, versus importing ruff's API or asserting complexity a different way, is design work for grooming.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Surfaced by a subagent running the plugin suite during PR #3165, 2026-08-23\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"fedf5afc0ab0bb0367c5e26e8e6b6d0b3a02b0ff844a9239db5c9d4623cd6a92\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQUHbFg\"}"}